E('rasputin|grigori rasputin', 'Grigori Rasputin was a Russian mystic who gained influence over the last tsar’s family.', 'He lived from 1869 to 1916.', 'He seemed to ease the bleeding of the tsar’s son, Alexei, who had haemophilia.', 'His influence scandalised Russian society.', 'He was murdered by nobles in 1916.', 'Legends say he survived poison and shooting before being drowned.')
E('nicholas ii|tsar nicholas|romanovs|anastasia', 'Nicholas II was the last Tsar of Russia.', 'He lived from 1868 to 1918 and reigned from 1894 to 1917.', 'He abdicated during the February Revolution of 1917.', 'He and his family were executed by Bolsheviks in July 1918.', 'Rumours that his daughter Anastasia survived were disproved by DNA tests.')
E('ho chi minh', 'Ho Chi Minh was the Vietnamese revolutionary leader of North Vietnam.', 'He lived from 1890 to 1969.', 'He declared Vietnam’s independence in 1945.', 'He led the fight against French colonial rule.', 'Saigon was renamed Ho Chi Minh City after the war.')
E('pol pot|khmer rouge', 'Pol Pot was the leader of the Khmer Rouge regime in Cambodia.', 'He lived from 1925 to 1998; the regime ruled from 1975 to 1979.', 'It forced people out of cities into labour camps.', 'Around 1.5 to 2 million people died.', 'Vietnam invaded and ended the regime in 1979.')
E('idi amin', 'Idi Amin was the military dictator of Uganda.', 'He ruled from 1971 to 1979.', 'He expelled Uganda’s Asian population in 1972.', 'His regime killed an estimated 100,000 to 500,000 people.', 'He was overthrown and died in exile in 2003.')
E('kwame nkrumah', 'Kwame Nkrumah led Ghana to independence.', 'He lived from 1909 to 1972.', 'Ghana became independent from Britain in 1957, one of the first sub-Saharan colonies to do so.', 'He was its first prime minister and president.', 'He championed Pan-Africanism.')
E('haile selassie', 'Haile Selassie was the last Emperor of Ethiopia.', 'He lived from 1892 to 1975 and ruled from 1930 to 1974.', 'He appealed to the League of Nations against Italy’s invasion in 1936.', 'He helped found the Organisation of African Unity.', 'He is revered in the Rastafari movement.')
E('desmond tutu', 'Desmond Tutu was a South African archbishop and anti-apartheid activist.', 'He lived from 1931 to 2021.', 'He won the Nobel Peace Prize in 1984.', 'He chaired the Truth and Reconciliation Commission.', 'He coined the phrase “Rainbow Nation”.')
E('simon de montfort', 'Simon de Montfort was an English noble who led a revolt against Henry III.', 'He lived from about 1208 to 1265.', 'In 1265 he called a parliament that included ordinary townsmen.', 'It is seen as an early step towards the House of Commons.', 'He was killed at the Battle of Evesham.')
E('thomas more|utopia', 'Sir Thomas More was an English statesman and writer.', 'He lived from 1478 to 1535.', 'He wrote Utopia, about an ideal island society.', 'The word “utopia” comes from his book.', 'He was executed for refusing to accept Henry VIII as head of the Church.', 'He was made a saint in 1935.')
E('guy fawkes|gunpowder plot', 'Guy Fawkes was one of the plotters in the Gunpowder Plot.', 'The plot was foiled on 5 November 1605.', 'Catholic conspirators planned to blow up the House of Lords and King James I.', 'Fawkes was caught guarding barrels of gunpowder beneath Parliament.', 'Bonfire Night is still celebrated in Britain on 5 November.')
E('william the silent', 'William the Silent led the Dutch revolt against Spain.', 'He lived from 1533 to 1584.', 'He is called the father of the Netherlands.', 'He was assassinated in 1584.', 'The Dutch national colour, orange, comes from his family, the House of Orange.')
E('frederick the great', 'Frederick the Great was King of Prussia.', 'He lived from 1712 to 1786 and reigned from 1740.', 'He made Prussia a major European power.', 'He was a talented flute player and composer.', 'He corresponded with Voltaire.', 'He encouraged potato farming.')
E('maria theresa', 'Maria Theresa was the only woman to rule the Habsburg lands in her own right.', 'She lived from 1717 to 1780 and ruled from 1740.', 'She reformed education and the army.', 'She had 16 children, including Marie Antoinette.')
E('garibaldi hero|giuseppe garibaldi', 'Giuseppe Garibaldi was an Italian general and hero of unification.', 'He lived from 1807 to 1882.', 'He led the “Expedition of the Thousand” to Sicily in 1860.', 'He also fought in South America.', 'He is called the “Hero of Two Worlds”.')
E('karl benz', 'Karl Benz was a German engineer who built the first practical automobile.', 'He lived from 1844 to 1929.', 'He patented his Motorwagen in 1886.', 'His company later became part of Mercedes-Benz.', 'His wife, Bertha, made the first long car trip to prove it worked.')
E('rudolf diesel|diesel engine', 'Rudolf Diesel was a German inventor of the diesel engine.', 'He lived from 1858 to 1913.', 'He patented his engine in the 1890s.', 'It was more efficient than steam engines.', 'He vanished from a ship crossing the English Channel in 1913.')
E('samuel morse|morse code|telegraph', 'Samuel Morse helped develop the electric telegraph and Morse code.', 'He lived from 1791 to 1872.', 'He sent the message “What hath God wrought” in 1844.', 'Morse code uses dots and dashes for letters.', 'SOS is · · · — — — · · ·.', 'He was also a painter.')
E('george stephenson', 'George Stephenson was an English engineer, the “Father of Railways”.', 'He lived from 1781 to 1848.', 'He built the Stockton and Darlington Railway in 1825.', 'With his son Robert he built the Rocket locomotive.', 'His track gauge became the world standard.')
E('isambard kingdom brunel|brunel', 'Isambard Kingdom Brunel was a British engineer.', 'He lived from 1806 to 1859.', 'He built the Great Western Railway.', 'He designed the Clifton Suspension Bridge.', 'His ship, the SS Great Britain, was the first iron, propeller-driven steamship to cross the Atlantic.')
E('alexander von humboldt|humboldt', 'Alexander von Humboldt was a German naturalist and explorer.', 'He lived from 1769 to 1859.', 'He explored Latin America from 1799 to 1804.', 'He saw nature as an interconnected whole.', 'More places and species are named after him than after almost anyone.')
